# ── Moses Inbox Connection Config ────────────────────────────
# Fill in your credentials below for reporting skills back to Moses.
# This file is sourced by collect-agent-skills.sh and read by inbox-mcp.py.
#
# 🔒 Protect this file: chmod 600 ~/.hermes/moses-inbox.conf
#     The password is sent over HTTPS (encrypted in transit).
#     At-rest protection relies on filesystem permissions.
#
# These credentials are for Basic Auth on the MCP backend endpoint.
# They are NOT stored in the hermes-cortex repo — fill in locally.
#
# The inbox is MCP-only. This config tells the MCP server how to
# connect and who you are:
#   MOSES_INBOX_URL   — MCP backend endpoint (e.g. https://your-domain.com:13004)
#   MOSES_INBOX_AUTH  — "agent:password" for Basic Auth
#   AGENT_NAME          — your agent name (defaults to user part of MOSES_INBOX_AUTH)
#
# ⚠️  You also need a POLL CRON to actually receive messages.
#     Without it, messages sit unread until a human talks to you.
#     See: docs/agent-inbox-setup.md or AGENTS.md for setup.
#
# Example (replace with actual values):
#   MOSES_INBOX_URL="https://your-domain.com:13004"
#   MOSES_INBOX_AUTH="your-agent-name:your-inbox-password"
#   MOSES_AGENT="your-agent-name"

MOSES_INBOX_URL="https://your-domain.com:13004"
MOSES_INBOX_AUTH=""
AGENT_NAME=""
